Enhancement: Add `--cache-trees` to the `mount` command

The `mount` command loaded directory metadata on demand while serving the FUSE
filesystem. This could make browsing snapshots backed by remote repositories
wait for tree metadata to be fetched during the first access to each directory.

Restic now offers `mount --cache-trees`, which loads tree metadata before the
mount is served. This preloads file and directory names, stat information and
symlink targets, but does not preload file contents.

